Below are the tests you must pass (see the exercise instructions for details).

Attached is a sample Makefile that demonstrates how to run the tests without having to copy your code files to the test directory. If the return value of a program is not 0, the make will stop runinig.
The makefile also demonstrates running the tests in different ways, such as valgrind or using diff.
You are welcome to review the Makefile and modify it to run them differently.
In the `SOURCE_DIR` variable, you must specify the path to your code directory, either as an absolute path or relative to the location of the Makefile.